Well, the major "problem" with your concept of
"avoidable" is that it means "avoidable if you know
of the specific problem in advance".

That makes it unworkable in the general case,
because there are too many _different_ potential
insta-death situations for there to be resources
available at any point in the early/middle game to
have catered in advance for _all of them at once_.

I'd like to suggest that any claimed cure for
"avoidable deaths" must be implementable to be
credible.

xanthian.

There are two possible approaches to "avoidable
deaths", IMO.

1) Know every edge case use of every resource so
that you can get out of situations in remarkably
sneaky ways.

2) Specialize in a small kit of resources (the kit
"to help you survive while assembling an AK") that
will counter all nasty situations in well known
ways, with high probability.

Everyone will have his/her definition of what that
latter kit of resources might contain.

I'm not limiting the concept to just physical
resources, but considering all the resources the
game provides.

One such abstract resource might be "always follow
your pet, and step only on squares on which your pet
(or a non-flying monster) has stepped, to avoid
traps".

Is that a proper resource to include in the above
kit?

Opinions will differ.

Examples are nearly endless.


